==Strategy==
It is recommended for the player to use Cat Units that have enough health to land some hits on the Crazed Lizard Cats before being killed (such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] or [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]]) and Cat Units that can outrange the Crazed Lizards (such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]). Other Crazed Cats like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] help immensely with this stage, if you happen to own them.

Additionally, it is possible to use the Mooths that spawn at the beginning of the stage to get enough money to rush the stage, and destroy the enemy base before the lizards even spawn.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]] is great here for cheesing the stage by defeating the base before the main bosses come out; and cost is not an issue with the initial Mooths. You may need higher levels depending on which unit you have and their own range.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] is actually able to ''outrange'' the crazed lizards, and deliver damage at a distance. However, if you bring him into the stage, do NOT use the regular Cat Cannon, or else he will run right into their range while the lizards are staggered and will be destroyed. Use the Slow Beam or Thunderbolt instead.

